  (text "FROM THE HAND-WRITTEN NETLIST THIS SHEET REPLACES (verbatim; the part notes are on each part's Note field):\n\nAUTHORITATIVE for connectivity. The ASCII drawing in power-entry-instrument.md is a REPRESENTATION of this\nfile. THE STRIP FEED AND THE ANALOG FEED ARE NOT SEPARATE NETS. The Interfaces table names them separately\nbecause they leave toward different circuits, but D-REVSHUNT is a shunt across the pair and D-TVS-PWR is a\nclamp, so nothing sits in series between J-UMB pin 3 and either tap. One node: UMBILICAL_POS12, all the way\nfrom the module's load switch to the WS2815 feed points and the REF5050's VIN. hardware/nets.yaml carried two\nextra entries for it until this file had to name both ends of each.\n\nDrawn here for context, owned by carrier/breath-excitation-reference: the REF5050 and its two 10 uF. They are\nin this drawing because the +12 V node feeds them, not because this circuit contains them.\n\nNO `value:` - the row is open and offers 1N5817 or SS14, one of the two.\n\nOne node: the umbilical's +12 V, the two shunts across it, the strip feed points, the REF5050 and both OPA2197\nhalves, and the buck inductor.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nTHE SINGLE TIE, and it is copper rather than a part. AGND_INST reaches PWR_GND at exactly one point on this\nboard - that is the whole content of the instrument half of dig-gnd-topology. On the board it is a net tie,\nNT-AGND: two nets that meet in copper at one place, which the layout's DRC then allows there and refuses\neverywhere else.\n\nThe far end is a 3 mm hole in an aluminium plate, not a net." (at 256.54 38.099999999999994 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid 084b05b0-c9b3-5308-81e0-03aee258b5a7))
  (symbol (lib_id "Transistor_FET:AO3401A") (at 40.64 142.24 0) (unit 1)
    (in_bom yes) (on_board yes) (dnp no)
    (uuid 16d59f65-9d6f-5d54-abb8-6b0ff937fe05)
    (property "Reference" "Q-INRUSH" (at 45.72 140.97 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)))
    (property "Value" "AO3401A" (at 45.72 143.51 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)))
    (property "Footprint" "Package_TO_SOT_SMD:SOT-23" (at 40.64 142.24 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) hide))
    (property "Datasheet" "" (at 40.64 142.24 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) hide))
    (property "Row" "Q-INRUSH" (at 40.64 142.24 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) hide))
    (property "Pins" "G=1(G) S=2(S) D=3(D)" (at 40.64 142.24 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) hide))
    (property "Note" "HOT-PLUG INRUSH LIMITER. P-channel, SOURCE AT THE CONNECTOR, drain to the instrument's bulk: its body diode points back at the connector, so nothing charges C-STRIP-BULK or C-BUCK-IN except through the channel, and the channel opens only as fast as C-INRUSH-GD lets the drain rise (power-entry-instrument.md, Hot-plug inrush). V_GS is +/-12 V max: the 1:1 divider holds it at half the input" (at 40.64 142.24 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) hide))
    (property "Pins_source" "datasheets/discrete-and-power/AOS-AO3401A.pdf p.1: SOT-23, pin 1 (by the dot) G, S and D as drawn; KiCad's AO3401A symbol numbers 1 G, 2 S, 3 D" (at 40.64 142.24 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) hide))
    (property "Manufacturer" "Alpha & Omega Semiconductor" (at 40.64 142.24 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) hide))
    (property "MPN" "AO3401A" (at 40.64 142.24 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) hide))
    (property "LCSC" "C15127" (at 40.64 142.24 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) hide))
    (property "Assembly" "machine" (at 40.64 142.24 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) hide))
    (pin "1" (uuid 98683813-4d64-5249-bb51-fdbaa6077a5b))
    (pin "2" (uuid 6c91822c-8223-5eba-8677-9a0eaf39939f))
    (pin "3" (uuid 4bd43a02-8766-5854-8496-5a0f54bfb132))
    (instances (project "main-board" (path "/b12a49ac-ffa0-5078-b2ba-e15d161f1936/4727eca5-0a6b-5761-98ac-51ca9f544ea2" (reference "Q1") (unit 1))) (project "power-entry-instrument" (path "/ba12e546-d582-5654-bb26-6a94a8f78514" (reference "Q-INRUSH") (unit 1))))
  )
